Jack: That sounds great, Mia. What kind of art is it?
Mia: It''s all about abstract painting. My art teacher says it''s amazing.
Jack: I''ve never really understood abstract art. Will we be able to understand it?
Mia: Don''t worry. There''s a free guide who explains the ideas behind each painting.
Jack: Perfect. What time should we meet?
Mia: Let''s meet at the museum gate at ten in the morning.
Jack: Ten o''clock is fine. I''m really excited now. See you on Saturday!', 'Mia 邀 Jack 周六去市博物馆看新展;是抽象画展,老师说很棒;Jack 担心看不懂抽象艺术;Mia 说有免费讲解员解释每幅画背后的想法;两人约定周六上午十点在博物馆门口见。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When will Mia and Jack go to the exhibition?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["On Saturday.","On Sunday.","On Monday.","On Friday."]},{"q":"What kind of art is the exhibition about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Stone sculpture.","Abstract painting.","Folk music.","Digital film."]},{"q":"Why does Jack feel a little worried at first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He may not understand abstract art.","He has no money.","He is feeling ill.","He does not like Mia."]},{"q":"How will they get help understanding the paintings?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They will read a long book.","A free guide will explain them.","They will phone the artist.","They will watch a film at home."]},{"q":"Where will the two friends meet?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["At the school library.","At Jack''s home.","At the museum gate.","At the train station."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
For some, childhood memories are the richest source of inspiration.
Others find new ideas while travelling to faraway places.
Many artists say that nature, with its colours and shapes, never stops inspiring them.
In the end, inspiration can come from anywhere, as long as we keep our eyes and hearts open.', '艺术家从哪里获得创意?答案因人而异;对一些人来说,童年记忆是最丰富的灵感来源;另一些人在远方旅行中找到新点子;许多艺术家说大自然的色彩与形状永远启发着他们;只要保持眼睛和心灵的开放,灵感可来自任何地方。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the passage mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How to sell famous paintings.","The price of modern art.","The history of old museums.","Where artists find their inspiration."]},{"q":"What is a rich source of inspiration for some artists?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Childhood memories.","Loud city noise.","Fast sports cars.","Crowded markets."]},{"q":"Where do some artists find new ideas?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["While sleeping all day.","While travelling to faraway places.","While doing the shopping.","While cooking dinner."]},{"q":"What never stops inspiring many artists?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Money and gold.","Television programmes.","Nature, with its colours and shapes.","Heavy traffic."]},{"q":"According to the passage, where can inspiration come from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only from school lessons.","Only from old books.","Only from famous teachers.","Almost anywhere, if we stay open."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Lily: Yes! The one made of metal wire and lights? It was breathtaking.
Tom: I agree. At night it looked like a giant fish floating in the air.
Lily: I heard the artist got the idea from an old folk tale.
Tom: Really? Which tale?
Lily: The story of a fish jumping through the Dragon Gate.
Tom: That''s clever. I was amazed that cold metal could feel so alive.
Lily: Me too. I think it''s the most creative work I''ve seen this year.', 'Tom 问 Lily 是否看过城市广场那座巨大雕塑;是金属丝和灯做的,很震撼;夜里像漂浮在空中的大鱼;Lily 听说灵感来自一个古老的民间故事——鱼跃龙门;Tom 惊讶冰冷的金属竟能如此有生命;两人都认为这是今年看过最有创意的作品。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was the sculpture made of?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Metal wire and lights.","Wood and paper.","Stone and sand.","Glass and water."]},{"q":"What did the sculpture look like at night?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A small singing bird.","A giant fish floating in the air.","A tall green tree.","A bright red car."]},{"q":"Where did the artist get the idea?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["From a science book.","From a strange dream.","From an old folk tale.","From a foreign film."]},{"q":"Which tale inspired the work?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A flying white horse.","A talking old tree.","A sleeping dragon king.","A fish jumping through the Dragon Gate."]},{"q":"How did Tom feel about the sculpture?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Amazed that metal could feel so alive.","Bored and very tired.","Angry about the high price.","Afraid of the bright lights."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
In the past, people had to travel far to see a famous painting.
Today, a digital version can be shown on a giant screen for everyone.
With 3D animation, the figures in an old painting seem to move and breathe.
In this way, great art has become more accessible to ordinary people than ever before.', '科技正在改变我们欣赏艺术的方式;过去人们要远行才能看到一幅名画;如今数字版可以在巨幕上向所有人展示;借助3D动画,古画中的人物仿佛会动、会呼吸;这样,伟大的艺术比以往任何时候都更贴近普通人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the passage mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["How to paint a perfect picture.","How technology changes the way we enjoy art.","The life story of one painter.","The price of large screens."]},{"q":"In the past, what did people have to do to see a famous painting?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Pay nothing at all.","Stay quietly at home.","Travel far to see it.","Wait for many years."]},{"q":"How can a painting be shown to everyone today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only inside a small book.","Only late at night.","Only to other artists.","As a digital version on a giant screen."]},{"q":"What can 3D animation do to figures in an old painting?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Make them seem to move and breathe.","Make them disappear completely.","Turn all the colours grey.","Make the painting much smaller."]},{"q":"What has happened to great art, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It has become much harder to see.","It has become more accessible to ordinary people.","It has lost all of its value.","It is now only for experts."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Sara: Mr Lee, can I write about the Floating Fish sculpture?
Teacher: Of course, Sara. Why did you choose it?
Sara: Because it shows how an old folk tale can inspire something modern.
Teacher: That''s a wonderful reason. Remember to describe how it makes you feel.
Sara: I felt amazed and a little moved when I saw it.
Teacher: Good. Use words like ''inspiring'' and ''breathtaking'' to express your feelings.
Sara: Thank you, Mr Lee. I can''t wait to start writing.', '老师布置写作任务:选一件给你深刻印象的艺术品;Sara 问能否写《漂浮的鱼》雕塑;老师问她为何选它;Sara 说它展现了古老民间故事如何启发现代作品;老师提醒她要写出自己的感受;Sara 说看到时既惊叹又有些感动;老师建议用 inspiring、breathtaking 这样的词表达感受;Sara 迫不及待要动笔。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is today''s writing task?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To paint a new picture.","To sing a folk song.","To write about an artwork that impresses you.","To build a small model."]},{"q":"Which artwork does Sara choose?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["An old stone bridge.","A short digital film.","A music recording.","The Floating Fish sculpture."]},{"q":"Why did Sara choose it?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It shows how an old tale can inspire modern work.","It was very cheap to buy.","It was extremely small.","It was easy to draw."]},{"q":"How did Sara feel when she saw the artwork?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Bored and sleepy.","Amazed and a little moved.","Angry and afraid.","Tired and unwell."]},{"q":"What kind of words does the teacher suggest using?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Numbers and dates.","Names of faraway cities.","Words like ''inspiring'' and ''breathtaking''.","Only the names of colours."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');
First, slow down and look carefully at the small things around you.
A leaf, a shadow or an old photo can all start a great idea.
Second, keep a notebook and write down anything that interests you.
Inspiration rarely arrives all at once; it grows from the details we notice every day.', '给任何想找到自己灵感的人一个简单的小贴士:第一,慢下来,仔细观察身边的小事物;一片叶子、一道影子或一张旧照片都能引出一个好点子;第二,随身带个本子,把任何让你感兴趣的东西记下来;灵感很少一下子到来,它从我们每天留意的细节中生长出来。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only world-famous artists.","Only school teachers.","Only young children.","Anyone who wants to find inspiration."]},{"q":"What is the first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Look carefully at small things around you.","Travel to other countries.","Buy expensive tools.","Copy other artists'' work."]},{"q":"What can start a great idea?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A very loud noise.","A leaf, a shadow or an old photo.","A fast-moving car.","A large, busy crowd."]},{"q":"What is the second piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sleep much more.","Watch more television.","Keep a notebook of what interests you.","Talk far less."]},{"q":"How does inspiration usually grow?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["All at once, without effort.","Only from our dreams.","Only from having money.","From small details we notice every day."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective1', 'U4', 'fltrp');

